  "description": "The existing garage is to be demolished and replaced with a two storey annex forming an extension to the main house. \n\nTo the front garden the existing concrete drive is to be repaved with cobblestones and seeded infill. The existing front wall is to repaired and extended. A paved hardstanding is proposed accommodate a timber slatted enclosure for an air source heat pump and wheelie bin store. \n\nTo the rear the existing single storey brick extension/WC building is to be demolished and replaced. \n\nTwo existing adhoc lean-to structures are to be replaced with a single storey brick extension. These structures are not original to the main house were constructed in an adhoc manner. They were in a dilapidated condition with asbestos sheet rooves. The lean-to structures are indicated on the existing drawings but have mostly been removed given safety concerns around structural stability and asbestos. With a total volume of 28cubic metres they fall below the 115cubic metre threshold for demolition within a conservation area without consent. \n\nA rear extension is proposed to replace the existing structures and provide a high quality living area that connects the house to he garden whilst providing a high levels of insulation and a green roof. To the east side of the rear an infill glazed conservatory structure is proposed to provide a garden room that still allows daylight to the principle living room behind. \n\nMinor service alterations are proposed as indicated on the facades to allow for altered drainage arrangement and an electric car charging point.\n\n\n",
